  "released": "1987",
  "notes": "This release has a \"Registered\" mark (®) near the label logos.  Other releases, such as [r=11988356] or [r=5662260], are very similar. \nIncludes brown paper record sleeves with the second catalog number printed on them.\n\n[On back sleeve:]\nRecorded in England from April 1983 – November 1986\nProduced tracks A1 and A4 for The BBC Radio 1 John Peel Show, released by arrangement with BBC Enterprises Ltd\nCover Star: Shelagh Delaney, reprinted from the Saturday Evening Post © 1961 Curtis Publishing Co\nReleased under licence from Rough Trade Records, England.\nMade in U.S.A.\n©1987 Sire Records Company\n℗1984, 1985, 1986, 1987 Sire Records Company\n\n[On liner:]\nMade in U.S.A. 9 25569-1\n\n[On labels:]\nA-side: ℗ 1987 Sire Records Company ℗ 1987 BBC\nA-side: ℗ 1984, 1985, 1986, 1987 Sire Records Company\nA-side: ℗ 1984, 1985, 1986 Sire Records Company\nA-side: ℗ 1984, 1985, 1986 Sire Records Company ℗ 1987 BBC\n\n[Additional runout information:]\nRunouts are hand-etched, except for the stamped parts 'SRC' and 'kdisc'.\n\nRegarding the \"vamp\" credit, Marr has stated \"On 'Ask'... I'm also vamping on a 'G' harmonica through a Urei Boom Box\".",
  "released_formatted": "1987",
